1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,626
For the second in our series about locally-run businesses, we meet Simon Winridge, co-founder

2
00:00:06,626 --> 00:00:10,260
of the hugely-successful Winridge Forest Railway Park.

3
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:11,385
Welcome, Simon.

4
00:00:11,385 --> 00:00:15,922
Now, perhaps you can begin by telling us a little bit about how it

5
00:00:15,922 --> 00:00:16,630
all started.

6
00:00:16,630 --> 00:00:22,569
Well, during the 1970s, my wife, Liz and I had just acquired 80 acres

7
00:00:22,569 --> 00:00:23,842
of sheep-farming land,

8
00:00:23,842 --> 00:00:27,660
and we decided to settle down and have children.

9
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:30,295
Pretty soon we had a daughter, Sarah,

10
00:00:30,295 --> 00:00:31,800
and a son, Duncan.

11
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:35,058
The place was wonderful for the kids:

12
00:00:35,058 --> 00:00:41,575
they particularly loved trains and gradually built up an enormous network of miniature railway

13
00:00:41,575 --> 00:00:42,040
track.

14
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:46,743
I began to develop larger-scale models of locomotives but we didn't think anything more

15
00:00:46,743 --> 00:00:51,446
of it until I went on a trip to a theme park near Birmingham

16
00:00:51,446 --> 00:00:54,470
and decided we could do a much better job!

17
00:00:54,470 --> 00:00:59,664
So we set up a small one ourselves based on the miniature railway

18
00:00:59,664 --> 00:01:05,257
and we opened to the public for just a month that year, 1984-in July-our

19
00:01:05,257 --> 00:01:10,851
driest month-because our children said they didn't want our guests to have a miserable,

20
00:01:10,851 --> 00:01:11,650
wet visit.

21
00:01:11,650 --> 00:01:16,910
I dealt with Park business and Liz carried on with the farm work.

22
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:21,510
It soon became clear that we were onto a winner.

23
00:01:21,510 --> 00:01:27,474
We began to extend the railway track and lay it among more interesting landscape

24
00:01:27,474 --> 00:01:28,752
by planting trees,

25
00:01:28,752 --> 00:01:31,308
which in turn attracted more wildlife,

26
00:01:31,308 --> 00:01:34,290
and by making cuttings through the rock.

27
00:01:34,290 --> 00:01:39,350
Nowadays, we're open all year round and we're pleased to say that Winridge is

28
00:01:39,350 --> 00:01:45,493
one of the most popular visitor attractions in the area-with 50,000 visitors a year - a million

29
00:01:45,493 --> 00:01:49,830
and a half people have been through our doors since we opened.

30
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:54,591
All these visitors mean we have had to expand our operation

31
00:01:54,591 --> 00:01:57,620
and it's now a truly family concern.

32
00:01:57,620 --> 00:02:02,743
I'm near to retirement age so I only concern myself with looking after the

33
00:02:02,743 --> 00:02:05,670
mechanical side of things - keeping the trains going.

34
00:02:05,670 --> 00:02:11,357
Liz now devotes all her energies to recruiting and supporting the large squadron of

35
00:02:11,357 --> 00:02:11,763
workers,

36
00:02:11,763 --> 00:02:14,200
which keep the place running smoothly.

37
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:19,539
We're really pleased that after some years away teaching, Sarah has now returned to the park

38
00:02:19,539 --> 00:02:22,877
and makes sure the visitors are kept fed and watered,

39
00:02:22,877 --> 00:02:25,880
which keeps her pretty busy as you can imagine.

40
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:30,486
Our son, Duncan, has been a stalwart of the park for the last ten

41
00:02:30,486 --> 00:02:33,776
years, taking over from me in the area of construction -

42
00:02:33,776 --> 00:02:37,724
and I'll say a little bit more about that in a moment -

43
00:02:37,724 --> 00:02:42,330
and his new wife, Judith, has also joined the team in charge of retail.

44
00:02:42,330 --> 00:02:47,930
That's becoming a tremendous growth area for us-a lot of people want to buy

45
00:02:47,930 --> 00:02:48,330
souvenirs.

46
00:02:48,330 --> 00:02:51,920
So have you finished your development of the site for the moment?

47
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:52,929
Not at all!

48
00:02:52,929 --> 00:02:56,630
We've constantly looking for ways to offer more to our visitors.

49
00:02:56,630 --> 00:03:02,863
The railway remains the central feature and there's now 1.2 kilometres of the line laid

50
00:03:02,863 --> 00:03:05,200
but we'd like to lay more.

51
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:10,280
Because of the geology of the area, our greatest problem is digging tunnels.

52
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:12,600
But we're gradually overcoming that.

53
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:18,053
We're also very pleased with a new installation of the GO-Kart arena which is

54
00:03:18,053 --> 00:03:20,000
120 square metres in area.

55
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,267
Again the problem is the geology;

56
00:03:22,267 --> 00:03:26,800
we had to level the mounds on the track for safety reasons.

57
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:30,938
We wanted to enable 5-12 year olds to use the go-karts.

58
00:03:30,938 --> 00:03:34,700
And the main attraction here is the Formula 1 Kart.

59
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:38,564
We've known fights to break out over who gets it!

60
00:03:38,564 --> 00:03:43,200
And then finally to our most recent development which is the landscaped…
